Logic & Explanation:
- Configured a macOS LaunchAgent /Users/vivek/Library/LaunchAgents/com.vivek.spare_token.plist with StartCalendarInterval set to 06:00 daily. macOS launchd natively coalesces and triggers missed calendar intervals immediately upon system wake when the MacBook lid is opened.
- Implemented wrapper script /Users/vivek/ICICI_Direct/MAC/run_spare_token.sh:
  1. Detects system wake and waits up to 60s for active network/Wi-Fi connectivity to prevent DNS/socket errors when contacting Google Sheets.
  2. Runs python3 /Users/vivek/Documents/nifty/data/index_options/credentials.nosync/update_spare_credentials.py to retrieve session token from Status_VM!G13 and update /Users/vivek/Documents/nifty/data/index_options/credentials.nosync/spare_credentials.json.
  3. Automatically syncs the retrieved session_token to the live copy /Users/vivek/Documents/nifty/data/index_temp.nosync/spare_credentials.json (mode 600) so downstream downloaders read the latest token.
  4. Appends execution status and timestamps to /Users/vivek/Documents/nifty/data/index_options/credentials.nosync/spare_token_run.log.
- Added Section 8 "macOS Scheduled Tasks & LaunchAgents" to /Users/vivek/ICICI_Direct/MAC/ubuntu_cheatsheet.md documenting how to disable, re-enable, and verify the task.
- Cleaned up obsolete user LaunchAgents: unloaded and removed com.vivek.nifty-breeze-download, ai.perplexity.*, and homebrew.mxcl.ollama.
- Updated memory note /Users/vivek/ICICI_Direct/memory/spare-token-updater-writes-backup-only.md and index in /Users/vivek/ICICI_Direct/memory/MEMORY.md.

